/-!
# The odd signalizer acts trivially on the full second flag space

A perfect odd nilpotent extension of SL₂(5) is generated by its five-elements.
For a binary representation of dimension at most six, normal prime subgroups
of its image modulo the two-core are central: the possible primes greater
than three are 5, 7 and 31, and the 7-subgroup has order at most 49. The
canonical radical commutator identity and two-perfectness then kill its
entire image, including the retained fixed layer of the original module.

The final two results construct a genuine odd Fitting prime for the remaining
nonquasisimple component. The companion SecondRadical module applies these
facts to the literal second normalizer; no irreducibility of full V₂ is used.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.1.2, printed p.765, with A.3.6 and 1.3.3,
combined manuscript of 1 March 2004.
-/

public noncomputable section
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory Representation
